# CPU baseline acceleration layer
# Cross-platform CPU-only ML baseline (no GPU-specific packages).
#
# This is a thin layer that ensures CPU-only execution.
# It includes ml-core.in and adds no GPU packages.
#
# Run `make compile` in this directory to generate pinned ml-cpu.txt
#
# Platform targets:
#   - darwin-x86_64-cpu   (macOS Intel)
#   - darwin-arm64-cpu    (macOS Apple Silicon, CPU fallback)
#   - linux-x86_64-cpu    (Linux Intel/AMD, CI baseline)
#   - linux-arm64-cpu     (Linux ARM)
#
# Capability contract:
#   - Cross-platform baseline (no platform-specific packages)
#   - No GPU acceleration packages (cuda-*, nvidia-*, triton)
#   - Install via: ./scripts/bootstrap/install_ml_stack.sh --profile core-cpu

# Include cross-platform ML baseline
-r ml-core.in

# CPU-only: no additional packages needed
# CUDA is a retired unsupported lane; MPS/CoreML are handled by their own
# Apple Silicon-specific layers.
